Ladybird now copies a selection as the text the page shows, with its
whitespace collapsed as rendered and with no text that isn’t visible,
which is what Selection.toString() already returned. Chrome 158,
Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5, run through their real copy and paste,
do the same: Each pasted “Read this as one sentence.” for a sentence
broken over source lines, and left out a “visibility: hidden” “¶”
link after a heading. They differ in what separates blocks (Chrome
pasted one newline between the heading and paragraph, Firefox and
WebKit two), which this change leaves as it was.
